     "<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Iriel Joerin<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, 2 September 2020 11:27<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> dartR &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">da...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> [dartR] gl.pcoa.plot.3d in presentations<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I would like to know if there is any way to export the 3d plots from gl.pcoa.plot.3d function to a presentation such as that from OpenOffice Impress or Power Point?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks a lot for your answer, <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Iriel<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div>"
